 Among the many good books on Descartes’s philosophy, I mention: Anthony Kenny,

 Descartes: A Study of his Philosophy (New York: Random House, ); Harry Frankfurt,

 Demons, Dreamers and Madmen: The Defence of Reason in Descartes’s Metaphysics (Indianapolis: BobbsMerrill, ); Bernard Williams,

 Descartes: The Project of Pure Enquiry (Harmondsworth: Penguin, ); E. M. Curley,

 Descartes against the Sceptics (Oxford: Blackwell, ); Margaret Wilson,

 Descartes (London: Routledge and Kegan Paul, ); John Cottingham,

 Descartes (Oxford: Blackwell, ).

 Recent collections of articles on Descartes’s philosophy include John Cottingham (ed.),

 The Cambridge Companion to Descartes (Cambridge: Cambridge University Press, ), Stephen Voss,

 Essays on the Philosophy and Science of Descartes (Oxford: Oxford University Press, ), and John Cottingham (ed.),

